<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle prices up $2-$3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle prices up $2-$3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>FEEDER CATTLE AUCTION:   250 head. Compared with two weeks ago, feeder</p>
<p>steers and heifers were mostly $2.00-$3.00 per cwt higher.</p>
<p>Overall quality below normal. Moderate buyer attendance.</p>
<p>Receipts 250  Last week  No report  Last Year  300</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 80.00-85.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 76.00-81.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 71.00-76.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:  700-900 lbs. 67.00-72.00</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS:  Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 72.00-77.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 69.00-73.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
